{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Fabric-Project/Fabric/pulls/407","id":4850296846,"node_id":"PR_kwDOOgxrpM8AAAABIRmoDg","html_url":"https://github.com/Fabric-Project/Fabric/pull/407","diff_url":"https://github.com/Fabric-Project/Fabric/pull/407.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/Fabric-Project/Fabric/pull/407.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Fabric-Project/Fabric/issues/407","number":407,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Publishing – A subgraph node owns its proxies, and is told each change as the change it is","user":{"login":"tobyspark","id":197773,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5Nzc3Mw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/197773?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tobyspark","html_url":"https://github.com/tobyspark","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tobyspark/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tobyspark/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tobyspark/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tobyspark/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tobyspark/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tobyspark/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tobyspark/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tobyspark/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tobyspark/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Genie –\r\n\r\n> Closes #400 · Supersedes the proxy fixes in #395 and #396\r\n> \r\n> 2 of 6.\r\n> \r\n> ### What it establishes\r\n> - The inner graph tells its `SubgraphNode` of each change through four events: `portDidPublish`, `portWillUnpublish`, `port(_:wasReplacedBy:)` and `portDidRename`. `onPublishedPortsChanged` and the after-the-fact proxy diff go.\r\n> - Several levels of publishing are handled by recursion through the public API. Proxy-chain state and `reattachConnections` are gone.\r\n> - `rebindWires(from:to:)` keeps each wire that `canConnect` allows and disconnects the rest, as undoable steps. Same-type replacements retarget the proxy in place.\r\n> - `Port.published` and `publishedName` are read-only outside Fabric. Changes go through `Graph.setPublished` and `setPublishedName`.\r\n> - Insert Parameter Node moves out of auto layout into a file of its own, and its publish transfer becomes undoable.\r\n> \r\n> ### Not in this PR\r\n> - Settings values, and the replaced-port tests that change a strategy (#3).\r\n> - Create Subgraph through the public API (#4).\r\n> - Clone members' own proxy ids (#6).\r\n> \r\n> ### Temporary lines\r\n> - `addDynamicPort`, `removePort` and `replacePort` raise the events. Declared ports replace them in #5.\r\n> - BaseImageNode's legacy port merge, which goes in #5.\r\n> - Two embedding lines, which go in #4.\r\n> - `proxyID(for:)` returns the inner port's id. It changes in #6.","created_at":"2026-10-13T22:28:35Z","updated_at":"2026-10-13T22:39:24Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"cad3019273597764ca00dd09a0585d5174e00f21","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Fabric-Project/Fabric/pulls/407/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Fabric-Project/Fabric/pulls/407/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Fabric-Project/Fabric/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Fabric-Project/Fabric/issues/407/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Fabric-Project/Fabric/statuses/f5f3ff13ca330ae3c855d43a9b73afd073eacabb","head":{"label":"Fabric-Project:stack/2-publishing-events","ref":"stack/2-publishing-events","sha":"f5f3ff13ca330ae3c855d43a9b73afd073eacabb","user":{"login":"Fabric-Project","id":207901582,"node_id":"O_kgDODGRTjg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/207901582?v=4","gravatar_